timegc_driver	^IN SPITBOL 1 GARBAGE COLLECTS REQUIRED A TOTAL OF \d+ MILLISECONDS TO FREE \d+ STORAGE UNITS\.$	CEO-409 (1)(a)+(b): TIME() differences and COLLECT() storage units, the engine clock and allocator (sbl 2464..3717 ms over six runs; FREED 38 in sbl -bf, 448 in SCRIP on the same program); K=1 is pinned by the drivers RESOLUTION stub and SYSTEM() by this regex, so neither is masked
timegc_driver	^THIS AVERAGES TO \d+\.\d*(e[-+]?\d+)?MSEC\. PER GARBAGE COLLECT AND \d+\.\d*(e[-+]?\d+)? MSEC\. PER STORAGE UNIT\.$	CEO-409 (1)(a)+(b): the two quotients of the masked line above, engine clock over engine storage units
timer_driver	^REQUIRED \d+\.\d*(e[-+]?\d+)? MILLISECONDS \+/- 10% TO EXECUTE IN SPITBOL$	CEO-409 (1)(a)+(b): wall-clock TIME() per execution (sbl 22.775 then 24.05 on two runs); SYSTEM() stays graded by the regex
